00:00:56.209 --> 00:01:01.299
NUMBER 3: Llewelyn Moss, from No Country for
Old Men, by Cormac McCarthy

00:01:01.299 --> 00:01:06.909
It’s 1980 an’ Llewelyn Moss out huntin’
in the Texas desert when he stumbles upon

00:01:06.909 --> 00:01:13.120
a satchel full of c-notes at a drug deal dat
went south. Dude’s an instant seven figure

00:01:13.120 --> 00:01:19.600
balla! Unfortunately, dat money puts him in
the crosshairs of Anton Chigurh, a savage,

00:01:19.600 --> 00:01:25.240
coin-flipping hitman hired to retrieve the
stolen loot. And this dude DON’T PLAY! If

00:01:25.240 --> 00:01:31.100
he say you dead, YOU DEAD. After sneakin’
back into the badlands to help out a dyin’

00:01:31.100 --> 00:01:36.719
man, things go from bad to worse for Llewelyn.
He’s chased across the desert, nearly iced,

00:01:36.719 --> 00:01:42.229
an’ sent to the hospital after a shootout
with the seemingly unkillable Chigurh. Man,

00:01:42.229 --> 00:01:48.200
I tell ya: that dog Anton is Shug Knight incarnate!
After hearin’ Chighur threaten to put one

00:01:48.200 --> 00:01:53.300
in his wife’s dome, Llewelyn busts his
ass to meet her in El Paso. Unfortunately,

00:01:53.300 --> 00:01:59.159
some Mexican hit-men smoke Llewelyn, and leave
his wife completely on her own against Chigurh.

00:01:59.159 --> 00:02:04.470
And dat boy Anton straight-up WASTES her just
fo’ being a third wheel in all this. Dayum!

00:02:04.470 --> 00:02:07.350
Dat s**t is COLD BLOODED!

00:02:07.350 --> 00:02:12.260
Llewelyn’s life went straight to s**t the
moment he brought home dat cheddar. But then,

00:02:12.260 --> 00:02:17.300
did it really? Some say his decision to help
that dying man back in the desert is what

00:02:17.300 --> 00:02:23.900
ultimately did him in. Maybe this is a sign
of who Llewelyn truly is: a good person who’s just

00:02:23.900 --> 00:02:28.849
not cut out for the thug life. Or maybe it’s
a warning dat there ain’t no stopping death

00:02:28.849 --> 00:02:34.200
for anyone, not even for decent folks like
Llewelyn an’ Mrs. Moss. If the cartels didn’t

00:02:34.200 --> 00:02:39.620
cap ‘em, Chigurh sure seemed determined
as the Devil to dust ‘em both. Could Llewelyn

00:02:39.620 --> 00:02:44.780
have skipped town wit all da moneys, or was
there no escaping his showdown wit death?

00:02:44.780 --> 00:02:49.490
Either way, Llewelyn tried to get outta Dodge
wit all the muscle his bankroll could buy

00:02:49.490 --> 00:02:54.830
him. And if dat kinda cash can’t duck the
Reaper, then we ALL f***ed!

00:02:54.830 --> 00:02:59.980
NUMBER 2: Jay Gatsby, from The Great Gatsby,
by F. Scott Fitzgerald

00:02:59.980 --> 00:03:04.560
When Nick Carraway lands a job in New York
City during the Twenties, he rents a shack

00:03:04.560 --> 00:03:11.400
next to the SWANK pad of Jay Gatsby, a mysterious
playboy who throws dope-ass parties but never

00:03:11.400 --> 00:03:16.780
joins them. It turns out Gatsby hosts these
ragers in the hopes of attracting his back

00:03:16.780 --> 00:03:22.349
when hunnydip: Daisy Fay, who lives across
the bay from Gatsby’s crib with her douchey

00:03:22.349 --> 00:03:28.659
old-money husband Tom Buchanan. After bein’
blue-balled for years, Jay and Daisy FINALLY

00:03:28.659 --> 00:03:34.280
start hookin’ up! Unfortunately, they do
a s**t job at keeping it from Daisy’s hubby,

00:03:34.280 --> 00:03:40.200
who gets his revenge by tellin’ her how
Gatsby made all his bucks bootlegging! YO!

00:03:40.200 --> 00:03:46.200
Dat boy Gatsby a hustla man! In another twist, Daisy decides to stick it out wit her deadbeat husband.

00:03:46.200 --> 00:03:49.720
Girl just can’t handle the thug life at Gatsby’s side.

00:03:49.720 --> 00:03:52.800
I thought you was a ride or die chick, Daisy.

00:03:52.800 --> 00:03:54.080
I'm disappointed.

00:03:54.080 --> 00:03:57.700
It looks like things couldn't be worse for Team Gatsby, until...

00:03:57.700 --> 00:04:02.260
HOLY S**T!
Tom's side b***h gets run over by Daisy! And

00:04:02.260 --> 00:04:07.859
da girl's husband thinks Gatsby was behind
the wheel! That dead chick’s crazy-ass hubby

00:04:07.859 --> 00:04:12.100
heads down to Gatsby’s mansion an’ BLASTS
him in his swimming-pool!

00:04:12.100 --> 00:04:14.700
It’s gameover for the Great Gatsby!

00:04:14.700 --> 00:04:18.000
Why did things
go south for great ol’ Gatsby? Maybe it

00:04:18.000 --> 00:04:22.470
was because his whole approach to life was
straight-up WHACK! Brutha thought he could

00:04:22.470 --> 00:04:27.980
buy his way back to happiness with a gangsta
wad, but Daisy ain’t one of his fancy ass shirts.

00:04:27.980 --> 00:04:33.600
That gal’s a human, and the human heart
ain’t the kinda thang you can buy on Amazon.

00:04:33.600 --> 00:04:36.800
You gotta go on the black market for that
kinda crazy s**t!

00:04:36.800 --> 00:04:43.300
Becoming rich didn’t make Gatsby any happier
than being rich did for Daisy. I mean just look at her!

00:04:43.300 --> 00:04:48.680
She’s a top-shelf socialite on the
surface, but her heart is busted, her marriage

00:04:48.680 --> 00:04:54.160
sucks, and she’s shallow as f**k. Even Nick
thought Gatsby’s corny-ass view of Daisy

00:04:54.160 --> 00:04:59.700
bein’ perfect wasn’t jivin’ with reality.
Neither character was capable of achieving

00:04:59.700 --> 00:05:05.200
the happiness they really wanted, which might be
why so many people compare The Great Gatsby

00:05:05.200 --> 00:05:10.040
to the failure of “the American dream.”
What is the American dream? Well it depends on

00:05:10.040 --> 00:05:14.831
who you ask, but it boils down to bustin’
yo’ ass ‘til you got enough bread to buy

00:05:14.831 --> 00:05:20.430
whatever make you happy. Does the American
dream hold up in practice? Well, in The Great Gatsby,

00:05:20.430 --> 00:05:26.570
the verdict is: “HELL NAW” All the American
dream got Jay Gatsby was a death sentence

00:05:26.570 --> 00:05:31.400
for vehicular homicide. Gee, thanks for driving,
Miss Daisy!

00:05:31.400 --> 00:05:36.669
NUMBER ONE: Bilbo Baggins, from The Hobbit,
by J.R.R. Tolkien

00:05:36.669 --> 00:05:42.400
Bilbo Baggins is a fatass hobbit who likes
to eat, blaze up, an’ do jack s**t-

00:05:42.400 --> 00:05:47.500
Till one day some nappy wizard crashed his crib
with a team of dwarves and invited him to

00:05:47.500 --> 00:05:52.700
retake the Lonely Mountain an’ all its treasure
from the dragon Smaug. DAYUM!

00:05:52.700 --> 00:05:55.700
Dat musta been some DANK Bilbo was chiefin!

00:05:55.700 --> 00:05:56.800
Oooooh!

00:05:56.800 --> 00:06:00.660
After some major
grubbin’, Bilbo joins the gang on a fantastic

00:06:00.660 --> 00:06:05.000
journey packed wit stranger thangs than we seen on Stranger THINGS! That we seen in Stranger Things!

00:06:05.000 --> 00:06:12.600
We’re talkin’ goblins, trolls, a magic ring dat Bilbo pockets, and an enormous dragon chillin’ atop a mound

00:06:12.600 --> 00:06:18.500
of shiny bling. Smaug gets his s**t wrecked
and the dwarves reclaim their mountain, but

00:06:18.500 --> 00:06:23.830
faster than you can say “My precious,”
five armies hustle over an’ start scrappin

00:06:23.830 --> 00:06:29.140
over the recovered loot! This result in the
climactic Battle of the Five Armies. Luckily,

00:06:29.140 --> 00:06:35.170
though , Bilbo ducks the drama and survives. The
lil’ shawty peaces out wit only a small

00:06:35.170 --> 00:06:40.830
purse as his prize money, but it’s all good.
He hurries home as fast as his fat legs can

00:06:40.830 --> 00:06:45.860
carry him, cause YOU KNOW where dat money’s
goin! Up in smoke, y’all!

00:06:45.860 --> 00:06:50.950
If you wonderin’ why Bilbo didn’t help
himself to more of the recovered swag, it

00:06:50.950 --> 00:06:56.520
might be because so much of the crazy s**t
in The Hobbit goes down cuz of good ol’

00:06:56.520 --> 00:07:01.990
fashioned greed. Consider the Dwarves’ obsession
to reclaim the mountain: something Thorin

00:07:01.990 --> 00:07:07.700
Oakenshield, leader of the dwarves, regretted
as he lay dying. “If more of us valued food

00:07:07.700 --> 00:07:12.820
and cheer and song above hoarded gold,”
he says to Bilbo, “it would be a merrier

00:07:12.820 --> 00:07:15.760
world.” Just about everyone in The Hobbit

00:07:15.760 --> 00:07:21.000
got their minds on the Dwarven treasure, which
might explain why Tolkien chose Bilbo as his

00:07:21.000 --> 00:07:26.920
main character. As a hobbit, there’s a childlike
innocence to him livin the simple life- unlike

00:07:26.920 --> 00:07:32.590
the dragons, dwarves, and orcs who all about
da money and da power. If Bilbo’s turned

00:07:32.590 --> 00:07:38.800
off by greed, that’s probably Tolkien’s
cue that we should as well. That said, Bilbo

00:07:38.800 --> 00:07:43.781
does f**k things up for Middle-Earth by swiping
that One Ring from the creature Gollum. Was

00:07:43.781 --> 00:07:49.071
this greed, or was it Tolkien setting up his
future books? What’s the difference? Cuz

00:07:49.071 --> 00:07:54.030
you know SOMEONE was seein’ dollar-signs
with that move! Shoutout to Pete Jackson!

00:07:54.030 --> 00:07:56.600
3 Hobbit movies? Boy please.

